t of a pung. But I only have one W5.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can form a pung of W1s. But I only have one W1. Not possible. So perhaps the only possible pung is the W8s.\n\nSo, if I pung W8, then I have that as a meld. Then the remaining tiles are W1, W2, W5, W9x2, T1, F2x2. Need two more melds and a pair. Let's see:\n\nMaybe a chow of W1, W2, W3 (no). Or maybe a pair of W9s. Then the remaining tiles are W1, W2, W5, T1, F2x2. Need two melds. Still not working. Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe there's a way to form a pung with T1? No, only one T1. What about the F2s? They are a pair. Then the remaining tiles are W1, W2, W5, W9x2, T1. Need two melds. Maybe a chow of W1, W2, W3 (no) and another chow? Not possible.\n\nThis seems tricky. Maybe I'm missing a possible meld. Let me list all the tiles again:\n\nHand: W1, W2, W5, W8x3, W9x2, T1, F2x2.\n\nMeld: [T4-T6].\n\nPossible melds:\n\n- Pung of W8s (3 tiles).\n\n- Pair of F2s.\n\n- Pair of W9s.\n\n- Pair of W8s (but three W8s can be a pung and a pair, but that would be five tiles, which isn't possible here).\n\nWait, if I pung W8s, that uses three W8s. Then the remaining two W8s would be part of the pair? No, because I only have three W8s total. So if I pung them, there's no W8 left. So the pair has to be elsewhere.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the pair is W9s. Then the remaining tiles would be W1, W2, W5, T1, F2x2. How to form two melds here? Maybe a chow of W1, W2, W3 (no) and a chow of W5, W6, W7 (no). Not possible.\n\nHmm. Maybe I need to discard a tile to make this work. The valid actions are to play F2, W1, W9, W8, W2, W5, or T1. Let's see which one to discard.\n\nIf I discard F2, then I have one F2 left. Maybe that helps in forming a pair later. But if I need a pair of F2s, discarding one would prevent that. Alternatively, if I discard W8, I lose the chance to pung, but maybe that's necessary.\n\nWait, maybe the problem is that I can't form the required melds with the current tiles. So perhaps I need to discard a tile that's not 